Table cms_cmsplugin {
  id integer [pk, increment]
  path varchar(255) [unique, not null]
  depth "integer unsigned" [not null]
  numchild "integer unsigned" [default: 0, not null]
  placeholder_id integer
  parent_id integer
  position "smallint unsigned" [default: 0, not null]
  language varchar(15) [not null]
  plugin_type varchar(50) [not null]
  creation_date datetime [not null, note: 'default in Python: now()']
  changed_date datetime [not null, note: 'default in Python: now()']

  indexes {
    (placeholder_id) [name: 'cms_cmsplugin_placeholder_id_0bfa3b26']
    (parent_id) [name: 'cms_cmsplugin_parent_id_fd3bd9dd']
    (language) [name: 'cms_cmsplugin_language_bbea8a48']
    (plugin_type) [name: 'cms_cmsplugin_plugin_type_94e96ebf']
  }

  Note: '''The base class for a CMS plugin model. When defining a new custom plugin, you should
store plugin-instance specific information on a subclass of this class.

An example for this would be to store the number of pictures to display in a galery.

Two restrictions apply when subclassing this to use in your own models:
1. Subclasses of CMSPlugin *cannot be further subclassed*
2. Subclasses of CMSPlugin cannot define a "text" field.

Columns from MP_Node (abstract): path, depth, numchild.'''
}

